Package: maxima
Title: Embed the 'Maxima' Computer Algebra System via 'ECL'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mitchell", "O'Hara-Wild", , "mail@mitchelloharawild.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Maxima developers", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Maxima computer algebra system, vendored and compiled at install time; see inst/COPYRIGHTS"),
    person("ECL developers", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "ECL (Embeddable Common Lisp) runtime, vendored and compiled at install time; see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
    )
Description: Embeds the 'Maxima' computer algebra system directly into R
    by linking a vendored, compiled 'ECL' (Embeddable Common Lisp) runtime
    with a vendored, compiled 'Maxima' core, avoiding any subprocess or
    text-protocol overhead. Calls into 'Maxima' are ordinary in-process
    function calls. Provides a thin, generic mechanism for calling any
    'Maxima' function from R and converting between R language objects and
    'Maxima' expressions, without imposing a curated high-level API.
License: GPL-2
Copyright: file inst/COPYRIGHTS
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    tools
Suggests:
    callr,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
LinkingTo:
    cpp11
SystemRequirements: A C/C++ toolchain (e.g. Rtools on Windows, Xcode
    Command Line Tools on macOS, build-essential on Debian/Ubuntu).
    No system ECL or Maxima installation is required: this package
    vendors and compiles both (and ECL's own bundled GMP, Boehm-GC and
    libffi) from source at install time. See tools/versions.sh for the
    exact pinned versions. GNU make, C99.
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
